## Hypothesis ID and title

**H-004 — JSON-LD vs. visible semantic HTML**

## Research question

Does structured data improve answer quality and entity understanding when the same information is already available in visible HTML content?

## Hypothesis statement

Adding consistent JSON-LD to equivalent visible content may improve entity extraction or relationship identification in some evaluated systems.

## Theoretical background

Structured data encodes explicit properties and relationships. Valid markup, consumer support, and downstream answer impact are separate propositions.

## Supporting literature and existing evidence

Not yet assessed; no evidence or source records are linked.

## Expected outcome

The HTML-plus-JSON-LD variant may produce measurable differences in entity or relationship extraction versus HTML alone; effect on answer quality and citations is unknown.

## Alternative explanations and potential counterarguments

Systems may ignore JSON-LD, rely on visible text, or use external sources. Results may reflect inconsistent markup, duplicates, or entity ambiguity.

## Validation approach

Verify parity and validity, compare visible-only, visible-plus-JSON-LD, and relationship variants under [EXP-003](/en/05-experiments/exp-003/).

## Related experiments and findings

- Proposed: EXP-003.
- Findings: none recorded.
